Write the scene script for the cast and topics below. It must read like a NATURAL conversation: each observer speaks in their own voice, reacts to what was just said, and probes in their own way. Never sound like a quiz; never mention mechanics.

Cast (id | name | personality | role):
{{ cast }}

Topics the player could have studied (id | name): {{ topics }}
Move tags the player will SEE: {{ tags }}
Scene turns: {{ turns }}

Hidden mechanics for each of the 4 options in a turn (the player never sees the kind):
- "commit": a specific claim about a topic; set "topic" to a topic id. It works if the player studied that topic; otherwise it becomes an improvised claim that a later check will catch.
- "evade": a vague, non-answer. Works early; fails after two evasions in a row.
- "risk": a bold, confident claim. It is the ONLY move that lowers doubt: "doubt_on_success" must be -1. It always counts as an improvised claim. Gate it with a condition.
- "redirect": turn the question back, or to someone else. Gate it with a condition.

Give each option:
- "text": the player's line, natural and in their voice (max 160 chars).
- "tag": one of the move tags (all 4 options in a turn must use 4 DIFFERENT tags).
- "kind": commit | evade | risk | redirect.
- "topic": a topic id for commit, otherwise null.
- "commits": claim ids this option asserts (commit and risk only). Name them like c_short_snake_case.
- "works_if": a list of 1-2 condition atoms, ALL of which must hold. Use ONLY these atoms:
  {"studied": topic_id} {"not_studied": topic_id} {"vague_streak_lt": n}
  {"target": cast_id} {"target_personality": "curious|skeptical|narcissist|formal|hostile"}
  {"claim_present": claim_id} {"claim_absent": claim_id} {"turn_lt": n} {"doubt_lt": n}
  (commit options use {"studied": its topic}; risk options usually require {"claim_present": an earlier claim} or a personality; redirect options use a personality or target.)
- "doubt_on_success" (0, or -1 for risk) and "doubt_on_fail" (1, or 2 for a failed risk) (integers -2..3).
- "line_if_pass" and "line_if_fail": the observer's natural reaction in their own voice (max 200 chars).
- "rationale": one short sentence explaining why it works or fails for THIS person right now (shown only in the review).

Rules the script must satisfy:
1. Exactly four options per scene node: one commit, one evade, one risk, one redirect.
2. THE WINNING MOVE MUST VARY. Across the scene at least THREE different kinds must be able to work, no kind may be the working one more than half the turns, and two consecutive turns must not have the same working kind. You control this through "works_if".
3. Every claim id in "commits" must appear in exactly ONE later check node: {"kind":"check","id":"c1","speaker":<cast id>,"claims":[claim ids],"line":"...","bluff_line":"...","confirm_line":"...","next":"..."}.
4. Linear chain: "n1" -> "n2" -> ... -> "c1" -> "c2" -> "end". Every non-end node has "next". Include one {"kind":"end","id":"end","line":"..."}.
5. "verdicts": one per cast id with "bought_it", "suspicious" and "sees_through" lines in that person's voice.

Keep it adult and fictional. Same content bans as before. No real institutions, no credentials, no forgery, no harmful detail.
